    "body": "Bumps [torchaudio](https://github.com/pytorch/audio) from 2.11.0 to 2.11.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/releases\">torchaudio's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>TorchAudio 2.11.1</h2>\n<p>This is a minor release with no new feature. It's compatible with PyTorch 2.11 and later.</p>\n<h3>Improvements</h3>\n<p>[packaging] Build a single <code>py3-none</code> wheel per platform, covering all supported CPython versions including free-threaded builds (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4224\">#4224</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4234\">#4234</a>)\n[packaging] Declare the <code>torch&gt;=2.11</code> dependency in the wheel metadata. It was previously unset (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4225\">#4225</a>)\n[packaging] Add the Python 3.15 classifier and <code>python_requires&gt;=3.10</code> to the wheel metadata (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4240\">#4240</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4224\">#4224</a>)</p>\n<p>[Documentation] <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4212\">#4212</a>\n[Code quality] <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4229\">#4229</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4231\">#4231</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4230\">#4230</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4232\">#4232</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4184\">#4184</a>, <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4179\">#4179</a></p>\n<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>\n<p>[CUDA] Only raise an error when torch and torchaudio were built with different CUDA major versions. Minor version mismatches are now allowed (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4226\">#4226</a>)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/455331b1b3bb4aabfe3228f6f911fc3f11ae93b1\"><code>455331b</code></a> [release/2.11.1] Add the Python 3.15 classifier to the wheel metadata (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4241\">#4241</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/26f10f68d3a619796b80194bd50acd407ec588c4\"><code>26f10f6</code></a> Prepare for 2.11.1 release (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4236\">#4236</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/239dad8132fbfe2ce9b6d2fa73382aea4e5c9bc1\"><code>239dad8</code></a> [2.11.1] Cherry-pick: Build a single py3-none wheel per arch x accelerator va...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/5f24fbbce55725e1cdf37e5901b1280666a8a1f5\"><code>5f24fbb</code></a> Build the docs on an OSDC runner (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4232\">#4232</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/45eaed85921bdab5348712a7e37db924bd150371\"><code>45eaed8</code></a> Move the Linux test jobs to OSDC runners (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4230\">#4230</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/7a0abb410a207e9a9b0f5f6f20e6309547d10c3f\"><code>7a0abb4</code></a> Build the Linux wheels on OSDC runners (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4231\">#4231</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/245ccb4118970340500e40f202fba8383636463e\"><code>245ccb4</code></a> Point the abi3 artifact pattern at 3.11 and fail loudly when it matches nothi...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/b85c99ccac635a06b1afaf5284bf4c1a00c1f9b5\"><code>b85c99c</code></a> Build a single abi3 wheel instead of one per Python version (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4224\">#4224</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/c3d51c3564a8d22674975e7dc1fc89d773f1f0d6\"><code>c3d51c3</code></a> dont error on CUDA mismatch for minor version (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4226\">#4226</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/commit/9c4849a6cf85e60e7ccf9fa068d9643b8b774a2f\"><code>9c4849a</code></a> set torch dep to torch&gt;=2.11 (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/audio/issues/4225\">#4225</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/pytorch/audio/compare/v2.11.0...v2.11.1\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility score](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=torchaudio&package-manager=pip&previous-version=2.11.0&new-version=2.11.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n\n\n</details>",
